[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mdeepseek_deepseek-v4-flash-failing-tests-trial-3[0m[0m
All 15 tests pass (`15 passed in 0.02s`), up from 10 failures. Only `src/` was changed; nothing under `tests/` was touched and no skips/xfails were added.

Bugs fixed:

- **`src/auth.py`** — `has_permission` compared roles case-sensitively (now case-insensitive via `.lower()`); `is_admin_or_owner` used `and` instead of `or` (admin alone or owner alone now grants access).
- **`src/inventory.py`** — mutable default `{}` shared storage across instances (now a per-instance copy); `add` overwrote instead of accumulating; `reserve` raised `OutOfStock` at the boundary `qty >= available` (now `>` so reserving exactly the available stock works); `release` allowed reserved count to go negative (now raises `ValueError`).
- **`src/text_utils.py`** — `slugify` kept original case and collapsed only one pair of separators per `replace` pass (now lowercases and collapses runs during iteration); `truncate` appended the suffix *on top of* `max_len` (now budgets the suffix into `max_len`).

Docstring examples in `slugify`/`truncate` were verified against the new behavior and still hold.
